    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d38">

                <pb facs="0170" n="85" sameAs="frus:frus1919v02/pg85"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">123C853/6b: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Commission to
                        Negotiate Peace</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-04-23T15:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">April 23, 1919,
                                3 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>1701. Crane took oath today. Understand he will be commissioned in Paris. Letter
                    of credence will be prepared here and <pb facs="0171" n="86" xml:id="pg86"/>
                    brought over by him for signature. Telegraph as soon as commission is signed so
                    passport as Minister may be issued.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Polk</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
